        ZmanMethod("sun-transit", "chatzos", "Sun Transit", false, false, false, false, false, explicitElevation = false, sourceMethod = "getSunTransit", hebrewLabel = "חצות שמש", definition = "Astronomical solar noon: the sun crosses the local meridian. Independent of the profile’s midpoint-versus-solar-noon choice.", sourceDefinition = "A method that returns sundial or solar noon. It occurs when the Sun is transiting the celestial meridian . The calculations used by this class depend on the AstronomicalCalculator used. If this calendar instance is AstronomicalCalculator) is set to use the com.kosherjava.zmanim.util.NOAACalculator (the default) it will calculate astronomical noon. If the calendar instance is to use the com.kosherjava.zmanim.util.SunTimesCalculator, that does not have code to calculate astronomical noon, the sun transit is calculated as halfway between sea level sunrise and sea level sunset, which can be slightly off the real transit time due to changes in declination (the lengthening or shortening day). See The Definition of Chatzos for details on the proper definition of solar noon / midday.") { c -> c.getSunTransit() },
        ZmanMethod("solar-midnight", "chatzos", "Solar Midnight", false, false, false, false, false, explicitElevation = false, sourceMethod = "getSolarMidnight", hebrewLabel = "חצות שמש בלילה", definition = "Astronomical lower-meridian transit at the end of the selected day. It can fall after civil midnight on the following date.", sourceDefinition = "A method that returns solar midnight as the end of the day (that may actually be after midnight of the day it is being calculated for). For example calculating solar midnight for February 8, will calculate it for midnight between February 8 and February 9. It occurs when the Sun is transiting the lower celestial meridian , or when the sun is at it's nadir . The calculations used by this class depend on the AstronomicalCalculator used. If this calendar instance is set to use the com.kosherjava.zmanim.util.NOAACalculator (the default) it will calculate astronomical midnight. If the calendar instance is to use the USNO Calculator, that does not have code to calculate astronomical noon, midnight is calculated as 12 hours after halfway between sea level sunrise and sea level sunset of that day. This can be slightly off the real transit time due to changes in declination (the lengthening or shortening day). See The Definition of Chatzos for details on the proper definition of solar noon / midday.") { c -> c.getSolarMidnight() },
        ZmanMethod("tzais-geonim8-point5-degrees", "nightfall", "Nightfall Geonim 8.5\u00b0 below horizon", false, false, false, false, false, explicitElevation = false, sourceMethod = "getTzaisGeonim8Point5Degrees", hebrewLabel = "צאת הכוכבים גאונים 8.5° below the horizon", definition = "Evening sun 8.5° below the geometric horizon. A solar angle, not a fixed-minute interval; the time may be unavailable at high latitudes.", sourceDefinition = "A method that returns tzais (nightfall) when the sun is 8.5° below the GEOMETRIC_ZENITH (90°) after sunset, a time that Rabbi Meir Posen in his the Ohr Meir calculated that 3 small stars are visible, which is later than the required 3 medium stars. This calculation is based on the sun's position below the horizon 36 minutes after getSeaLevelSunrise() sunset in Jerusalem around the equinox / equilux , which is 8.5° below GEOMETRIC_ZENITH.") { c -> c.getTzaisGeonim8Point5Degrees() },
        ZmanMethod("alos16-point1-degrees", "dawn", "Dawn 16.1\u00b0 below horizon", false, false, false, false, false, explicitElevation = false, sourceMethod = "getAlos16Point1Degrees", hebrewLabel = "עלות השחר 16.1° below the horizon", definition = "Morning sun 16.1° below the geometric horizon. A solar angle, not a fixed-minute interval; the time may be unavailable at high latitudes.", sourceDefinition = "Returns alos (dawn) based on the time when the sun is 16.1° below the eastern GEOMETRIC_ZENITH before sunrise. This is based on the calculation that the time between dawn and sunrise (and sunset to nightfall) is 72 minutes, the time that is takes to walk 4 mil at 18 minutes a mil ( Rambam and others). The sun's position below the horizon 72 minutes before sunrise in Jerusalem on the around the equinox / equilux is 16.1° below GEOMETRIC_ZENITH.") { c -> c.getAlos16Point1Degrees() },
        ZmanMethod("alos72-minutes", "dawn", "Dawn 72 minutes", false, false, false, true, false, explicitElevation = false, sourceMethod = "getAlos72Minutes", hebrewLabel = "עלות השחר 72 minutes", definition = "72 fixed clock minutes before sunrise. Sunrise/sunset follow the profile elevation policy.", sourceDefinition = "Method to return alos (dawn) calculated as 72 minutes before sunrise or getSeaLevelSunrise() sea level sunrise (depending on the isUseElevation() setting). This time is based on the time to walk the distance of 4 mil at 18 minutes a mil. The 72-minute time (but not the concept of fixed minutes) is based on the opinion that the time of the Neshef (twilight between dawn and sunrise) does not vary by the time of year or location but depends on the time it takes to walk the distance of 4 mil.") { c -> c.getAlos72Minutes() },
        ZmanMethod("chatzos-hayom", "chatzos", "Midday", false, false, false, false, false, explicitElevation = false, sourceMethod = "getChatzosHayom", hebrewLabel = "חצות היום", definition = "Uses astronomical solar noon when the profile enables it; otherwise uses the midpoint of sea-level sunrise and sunset, with the pinned library’s astronomical fallback when needed.", sourceDefinition = "This method returns Astronomical chatzos hayom if the calculator class used supports it and isUseAstronomicalChatzos() is set to true or the halfway point between sunrise and sunset if it does not support it, or it is not configured to use it. There are currently two calculators available in the API, the default com.kosherjava.zmanim.util.NOAACalculator NOAA calculator and the USNO calculator. The USNO calculator calculates chatzos as halfway between sunrise and sunset (identical to six shaos zmaniyos after sunrise), while the NOAACalculator calculates it more accurately as astronomical chatzos . See The Definition of Chatzos for a detailed explanation of the ways to calculate Chatzos . Since half-day chatzos can be null in the Arctic on a day when either sunrise or sunset did not happen and astronomical chatzos can be calculated even in the Arctic, if half-day chatzos calculates as null and astronomical chatzos is supported by the calculator, astronomical chatzos will be returned to avoid returning a null .") { c -> c.getChatzosHayom() },
        ZmanMethod("chatzos-halayla", "chatzos", "Midnight", false, false, false, false, false, explicitElevation = false, sourceMethod = "getChatzosHalayla", hebrewLabel = "חצות הלילה", definition = "Midnight at the end of the selected day. Uses astronomical midnight when enabled; otherwise the midpoint of sea-level sunset and the following sunrise, with astronomical fallback if needed.", sourceDefinition = "A method that returns chatzos halayla at the end of the day (the last zman of the day returned by the calendar, that may actually be after midnight of the day it is being calculated for). For example, if calculating it for the date of Erev Pesach , the calculation will be for Lail Pesach to allow you to use the zman as sof zman achilas afikoman . Astronomical chatzos halayla will be returned if the calculator class used supports it and isUseAstronomicalChatzos() isUseAstronomicalChatzos() is set to true . Otherwise the Instant) halfway point between sunset and the following day's sunrise, if it does not support it, or it is not configured to use it. There are currently two calculators available in the API, the default NOAA calculator and the com.kosherjava.zmanim.util.SunTimesCalculator USNO calculator. The USNO calculator calculates chatzos halayla as halfway between sunset and the following day's sunrise (identical to six shaos zmaniyos after sunset), while the NOAACalculator calculates it more accurately as astronomical chatzos halayla . See The Definition of Chatzos for a detailed explanation of the ways to calculate Chatzos . Since half-night chatzos can be null in the Arctic on a day when either sunset or the following day's sunrise did not happen and astronomical chatzos halayla can be calculated even in the Arctic, if half-day chatzos calculates as null and astronomical chatzos is supported by the calculator, astronomical chatzos will be returned to avoid returning a null .") { c -> c.getChatzosHalayla() },
        ZmanMethod("chatzos-hayom-as-half-day", "chatzos", "Midday As Half Day", false, false, false, false, false, explicitElevation = false, sourceMethod = "getChatzosHayomAsHalfDay", hebrewLabel = "חצות היום As Half Day", definition = "The midpoint of sea-level sunrise and sunset, independently of the profile’s astronomical-noon switch.", sourceDefinition = "Returns chatzos calculated as halfway between sunrise and sunset. Many are of the opinion that chatzos is calculated as the midpoint between sea level sunrise and sea level sunset, despite it not being the most accurate way to calculate it. A day starting at alos and ending at tzais using the same time or degree offset will also return the same time. In reality due to lengthening or shortening of day, this is not necessarily the exact midpoint of the day, but it is very close. This method allows you to use the NOAACalculator and still calculate chatzos as six shaos zmaniyos after sunrise. There are currently two com.kosherjava.zmanim.util.AstronomicalCalculator calculators available in the API, the com.kosherjava.zmanim.util.NOAACalculator and the com.kosherjava.zmanim.util.SunTimesCalculator. The SunTimesCalculator calculates chatzos as halfway between sunrise and sunset (and of six shaos zmaniyos ), while the NOAACalculator calculates it as astronomical chatzos that is slightly more accurate. This method allows you to use the NOAACalculator and still calculate chatzos as six shaos zmaniyos after sunrise. See The Definition of Chatzos for a detailed explanation of the ways to calculate Chatzos .") { c -> c.getChatzosHayomAsHalfDay() },
